-- M4 Stage A, gate PASS-M4A-SX.  A one-constructor family whose sole
-- argument is erased (quantity 0) but SELF-RECURSIVE (wrap : (0 s : SX)
-- -> SX) stays Kernel.Erased_use: the subsingleton criterion's third
-- clause (not self-recursive) is the fence here, not a quantity.  Note
-- that "data SX" itself is ACCEPTED (M2 positivity has no complaint);
-- only the eliminating def sxLoop is rejected, at the STAMP (zero_
-- eliminable fails on self_rec), not by any runtime mechanism.  A
-- regression that flips this to check would let the M2 fixes Round 4
-- erased-guard soundness argument's relaxation (see A6.6 in
-- lib/check.ml) go unchecked.
data SX : Type 0 := | wrap : (0 s : SX) -> SX
def rec sxLoop : (0 s : SX) -> Nat := fun s => match s with | wrap s2 => sxLoop s2 end
